From 24a4da583425a0fc56322e82ddb800d43bbfbc84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:24:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 105/110] Killboard and battle reports

Opening a kill mail in Crucible only shows the plain text list, and the
client's UI can't be changed, so the server serves a kill report, a
zKillboard-style board and battle reports as web pages, from the image
server at http://<server>:26001/kb/.  They open in the in-game browser
(show info links work there) and in any normal browser.  Everyone
involved in a kill gets a CONCORD mail with a link to its report, and
/killboard (or /kb) answers with links to the recent kills, your own
kills and losses, and the battle reports.

Fixes rolled in:
- the star map's kill counts stop at 32,767 instead of failing the
  update
- the star map's jumps in the last hour start again every hour (they
  only ever went up)
